# S-050 nvenc: capability table from the obs-nvenc-test helper process. The helper prints an INI
# document on stdout; nvenc_check() parses it. Keys per codec section: codec_supported (bool, if
# false nothing else is read for that codec), bframes bref engines max_width max_height
# temporal_filter lookahead_level (ints), dynamic_bitrate lookahead lossless temporal_aq 10bit
# yuv_444 yuv_422 uhq (bools). [general]: nvenc_supported nvenc_devices nvenc_ver cuda_ver driver_ver.
# The driver's major version decides has_broken_split_encoding (< 555).
ini "[general]\nnvenc_supported=true\nnvenc_devices=2\nnvenc_ver=13.0\ncuda_ver=12.8\ndriver_ver=555.85\n[h264]\ncodec_supported=true\nbframes=4\nbref=3\nengines=2\nmax_width=4096\nmax_height=4096\ntemporal_filter=1\nlookahead_level=2\ndynamic_bitrate=true\nlookahead=true\nlossless=true\ntemporal_aq=true\n10bit=true\nyuv_444=true\nyuv_422=false\nuhq=true\n[hevc]\ncodec_supported=true\nbframes=2\nbref=1\nengines=1\nmax_width=8192\nmax_height=8192\ndynamic_bitrate=true\n10bit=true\n[av1]\ncodec_supported=false\nbframes=9\n"
supported
caps h264
caps hevc
caps av1
vinfo
brokensplit
props h264
props av1
